{% extends 'AdminInterfaceBundle:Layout:list.html.twig' %}
{% block listpane_content %}

	<section class="dp-paneblock dp-listpane">
		<header>
			<nav>
				<span dp-ping-flash="run_orders" class="saved-ping"><i class="fa fa-check-square-o-square"></i> {{ phrase('agent.general.saved') }}</span>
				{% include 'AdminInterfaceBundle:Layout:standard-settings-menu.html.twig' %}
			</nav>
			<h3 ng-pluralize count="List.webhooks.length" when="{{ ng_plural_phrase('adm.ticket_webhooks.count_webhooks') }}"></h3>
		</header>

		<article>
			<p ng-if="!List.webhooks.length" style="padding: 15px;">
                {{ phrase('adm.ticket_webhooks.no_webhooks') }}
			</p>
			<ul class="dp-item-list" ng-if="List.webhooks.length" dp-max-height>

				<li class="with-drag-handle" ng-repeat="webhook in List.webhooks" dp-state-mark="id:tickets.webhooks.edit.{{ ng_var('webhook.id') }}" data-webhook-id="{{ ng_var('webhook.id') }}" data-run-order="{{ ng_var('webhook.id') }}">
					<div class="link">

						<div class="pull-right toggle-wrapper">
							<button dp-toggle-switch ng-model="webhook.is_enabled" ng-change="List.changeEnabledStatus(webhook);"></button>
						</div>

						<div class="pull-right toggle-wrapper">
							<button ng-click="List.addTrigger(webhook);"><i class="fa fa-plus"></i></button>
						</div>

						<a href="{{ ng_href('tickets.webhooks.edit', '{id: webhook.id}') }}">
							<h4>
								<span class="title-id" title="ID">#{{ ng_var('webhook.id') }}</span>
								<span class="title-text">{{ ng_var('webhook.title') }}</span>
							</h4>
						</a>

					</div>

					<ul class="dp-item-list sublist ui-sortable" ng-show="webhook.triggers.length" dp-max-height>


						<li class="with-drag-handle ng-scope" ng-repeat="trigger in webhook.triggers" dp-state-mark="id:tickets.triggers.edit.{{ ng_var('trigger.id') }}" data-trigger-id="{{ ng_var('trigger.id') }}" data-run-order="{{ ng_var('trigger.run_order') }}">
							<a href="{{ ng_href('tickets.webhooks.trigger-edit', '{webhookId: webhook.id,  id: trigger.id}') }}">

								<i class="fa fa-bars drag-handle"></i>

								<div ng-if="trigger.has_stop_triggers_action" class="pull-right" title="This trigger has a &quot;stop processing triggers&quot; action. When this trigger matches, any trigger after it will NOT be run.">
									<i class="fa fa-chain-broken"></i>
								</div>
								<div ng-if="trigger.has_delete_ticket_action" class="pull-right" title="This trigger has a &quot;delete ticket&quot; action. When this trigger matches, the ticket will be deleted and any trigger after it will NOT be run.">
									<i class="fa fa-chain-broken"></i>
								</div>

								<div class="pull-right toggle-wrapper">
									<button dp-toggle-switch ng-model="trigger.is_enabled" ng-change="List.changeEnabledStatusTrigger(trigger);"></button>
								</div>

								<h4>
									<span class="tree-char middle" ng-if="!$last"></span>
									<span class="tree-char last" ng-if="$last"></span>
									<span class="title-id" title="ID">#{{ ng_var('trigger.id') }}</span>
									<span class="title-text">{{ ng_var('trigger.title') }}</span>
								</h4>
							</a>
						</li>
					</ul>


				</li>


			</ul>
			<div class="dp-add-control">
				<a class="btn btn-default" href="{{ ng_href('tickets.webhooks.create') }}" ng-class="{'active': isStateActive('.create') }"><i class="fa fa-plus"></i> {{ phrase('agent.general.add') }}</a>
			</div>
		</article>

	</section>
{% endblock %}
{% block listpane_help %}
	<header>

		<h1>Triggers are automatic processes that can perform actions in response to ticket events.</h1>
		<p ng-if="List.eventType == 'newreply'">Triggers in this section are checked every time a <strong>new reply</strong> is made by a user or agent.</p>
		<p ng-if="List.eventType == 'newticket'">Triggers in this section are checked every time a <strong>new ticket</strong> is created.</p>
		<p ng-if="List.eventType == 'update'">Triggers in this section are checked when a ticket is <strong>updated</strong>.</p>

	</header>

	<article>
		<section>


				<p>Triggers have <strong>criteria</strong> they check before they run their defined <strong>actions</strong>.</p>

				<p>The triggers are checked in order from the top down. You can drag them to change the order.</p>


<h2>Simple triggers</h2>

				<p>DeskPRO automatically creates <strong>Department Triggers</strong> for each of your departments. They run when a user creates a ticket in the matching department via the web.</p>



				<p>There are also <strong>Email Account Triggers</strong> that run when a user submits a ticket via the matching email account.</p>

				<p>You can change the actions on these triggers to quickly carry out simple configuration changes like:</p>

					<ul>
						<li>assigning all tickets from an email account to a particular agent</li>
						<li>sending different acknowledgement emails based on department</li>

					</ul>

				<p>You can also view and edit these triggers from <strong>Tickets > Departments</strong> and <strong>Tickets > Email Accounts</strong>.</p>


	<h2> Advanced triggers</h2>



			<p>For advanced triggers, you can use the <strong>Event</strong> section to refine when the trigger is checked. You can choose to have the trigger respond only to user actions or only to agent actions; or to respond only to certain interfaces (email, web, the API etc.).</p>

			<p>If you are using an advanced trigger to send a response email, don't forget to disable the corresponding simple triggers to avoid sending the same email twice.</p>


			<p><strong>Actions</strong> can automatically do most of the things you would do to a ticket in the agent interface.</p>


			<p>Special <strong>Trigger Control</strong> actions can affect any following triggers lower in the list. The <em>Stop Processing Triggers</em> action prevents following triggers running. You can also use <em>Prevent Emails to User</em> or <em>Prevent Emails to Agents</em> to stop any email notifications that lower triggers try to send. These only prevent triggers that are running immediately afterwards - i.e. that are being checked due to the same event.

			</p>


	<h2> SMS triggers </h2>
	<p> Note that to send SMS alerts, you must have an account with an SMS delivery provider, and install the corresponding app in the <strong>Apps</strong> section.</p>

	<p>For SMS delivery to work, ensure that the receiving agent's cell/mobile number has been entered in their profile in the <strong>Agents</strong> section of this interface (not the CRM section in the agent interface).</p>



		</section>

		<section>

			<h2><span>FAQ</span></h2>

			<dl>
				<dt><em>Q:</em>My triggers aren't behaving as I expect. How do I troubleshoot them?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
				You can see which triggers ran and in what order using the ticket <strong>Full Log</strong> tab in the agent interface.
				</dd>

				<dt><em>Q:</em>What does Check Current Agent do in trigger criteria?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
				This checks if the agent or agents selected caused the event, whether through the agent interface, while logged in to the portal or via email.
				</dd>


				<dt><em>Q:</em>What does Check Performer Email do in trigger criteria?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
				This checks the email address of the person who caused the event, whether they are a user or an agent.
				</dd>

				<dt><em>Q:</em>When using a Set Assigned Team action, what does "the Current Agent's team" do if the agent has multiple teams?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
				It uses the agent's <strong>primary team</strong>, as set in their profile under <strong>Agents</strong>.
				</dd>

			</dl>



		</section>

		<section class="related-content">
		<h2><span>Related Content</span></h2>
		<ul>
			<li><i class="fa fa-book"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/guides/topic/374" target="_blank">Ticket triggers</a>
			<li><i class="fa fa-book"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/guides/topic/383" target="_blank">Actions guide</a>
			<li><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/kb/articles/192" target="_blank">Send an email to the user when their ticket is assigned</a></li>
			<li><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/kb/articles/193" target="_blank">Sending different auto-responses based on email address</a></li>
			<li><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/kb/articles/194" target="_blank">Automatically assign agents to tickets they reply to by email</a></li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</article>
{% endblock %}
